From e1007aff0fb5b3beb5d622ddf04be7188cce268c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ole Algoritme <olealgoritme@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 21:23:55 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 04/13] nvk/rm: logical device and memory

Each nvkmd_rm_dev opens its own RM client with its own NV01_DEVICE_0 and
NV20_SUBDEVICE_0, and sets up:

  - a FERMI_VASPACE_A (64 KiB big pages) with VA_INTERNAL_LIMIT, so RM's
    internal mappings stay in [4 GiB, 4.5 GiB), which is carved out of
    NVK's VA heap,
  - the usermode doorbell region (VOLTA..BLACKWELL_USERMODE_A, BAR1,
    write-only) mapped through the subdevice,
  - if librmclient has crm_event_open, an OS event on the FIFO non-stall
    interrupt (without event data, the payload is not needed and Conduit
    guests cannot read it), for CPU waits later,
  - the GPU timestamp via NV2080_CTRL_CMD_TIMER_GET_TIME.

Memory:
  - CPU-mappable and GART memory is our own anonymous pages wrapped in
    NV01_MEMORY_SYSTEM_OS_DESCRIPTOR: the CPU map is the allocation
    itself.  RM-allocated NV01_MEMORY_SYSTEM is the fallback.
  - Device-local memory is NV01_MEMORY_LOCAL_USER with 64 KiB pages.
  - Explicit VRAM | CAN_MAP is mapped through BAR1 with crm_map_memory.
  - All memory is coherent; no dma-buf, tiled BOs, fixed maps or
    overmaps.

GPU VA and contexts are still stubs.
